  "term": "feeling of reality",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, the feeling of reality is the sense that events and one’s choices are genuinely being decided from moment to moment. It refers to the vivid, consequential quality of voluntary life, as opposed to feeling that everything is merely unfolding in a fixed, predetermined way.",
